==English==
{{was wotd|2006|June|9}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|sollicit||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*solh₂-|*keyh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|soliciten}}, {{m|enm|solliciten}}, from {{der|en|fro|soliciter}}, {{m|fro|solliciter}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|sollicitō|t=stir, disturb; look after}}, from {{m|la|sollicitus|t=agitated, anxious, punctilious|lit=thoroughly moved}}, from {{m|la|sollus|t=whole, entire}} + perfect passive participle of {{m|la|cieō|t=shake, excite, cite, to put in motion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sə-lĭs'ĭt}}, {{IPA|en|/səˈlɪsɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-solicit.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-solicit.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪsɪt|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[persistent]]ly [[endeavor]] to [[obtain]] an object, or [[bring about]] an event.
#: {{syn|en|supplicate|thig}}
#: {{cot|en|pester|beg|agitate}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''solicit''' alms, or a favour}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Works|title=Eloisa to Abelard|passage=I view my crime, but kindle at the view, <br> Repent old pleasures, and '''solicit''' new.<br>Did I '''solicit''' thee From darkness to promote me?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[woo]]; to [[court]].
#: {{syn|en|address|romance}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[persuade]] or [[incite]] one to [[commit]] some act, especially [[illegal]] or [[sexual]] [[behavior]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=8|passage=That fruit {{...}} '''sollicited''' her longing eye.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Human Understanding}}, Book II, Chapter 1
#: {{ux|en|If you want to lose your virginity, you should try to '''solicit''' some fine looking women.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[offer]] to [[perform]] [[sexual]] [[activity]], especially when for a [[payment]].
#: {{ux|en|My girlfriend tried to '''solicit''' me for sex, but I was tired.}}
# To make a [[petition]].
#: {{syn|en|appeal|petition|request}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|transitive}} To [[disturb]] or [[trouble]]; to [[harass]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[urge]] the [[claim]]s of; to [[plead]]; to act as [[solicitor]] for or with [[reference]] to.
#: {{syn|en|plead}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1628|author={{w|John Ford (dramatist)|John Ford}}|title=w:The Lover's Melancholy
|passage=Should <br> My brother henceforth study to forget <br> The vow that he hath made thee, I would ever <br> '''Solicit''' thy deserts.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|rare|transitive}} To [[disturb]]; to [[disquiet]].
#: {{syn|en|worry}}
#* '''1611-1615''', {{w|George Chapman}}, ''{{w|Iliad}}'', Book XVI
#* {{RQ:Dryden Spanish Fryar|3|2
|passage=But anxious fears '''solicit''' my weak breast.}}

